<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="sec-divide" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Dividing Fractions</title>

<p> When dividing fractions, we first turn the problem into one of multiplication by taking the reciprocal of the second fraction;
  <md>\frac{a}{c}\div\frac{b}{d}=\frac{a}{c}\times\frac{d}{b}.</md>
Since the previous section looked at multiplication of fractions, this is now a problem we know how to solve. </p>


  <example>
    <title>Dividing Fractions</title>
    <statement>
      <p>
        Calculate <m>\frac{5}{7}\div\frac{4}{9}</m>.
      </p>
    </statement>
    <solution>
      <p>
        We first convert the problem to one of multiplication; 
         <md>\frac{5}{7}\div\frac{4}{9}=\frac{5}{7}\times\frac{9}{4}=\frac{5\times 9}{7\times 4}=\frac{45}{36}.</md>
         This is in reduced form.
      </p>
    
    </solution>
  </example>

  <exercise label="ww-fraction-division">
    <title>Dividing Fractions</title>
    <webwork>
        <pg-code>
            # Set the math environment to expect fraction format answers
            Context("Fraction-NoDecimals");
            
            # Define the exact answer
            $ans = Fraction(40,27);
        </pg-code>
        <statement>
            <p>
                Evaluate the following expression. 
                Provide your answer as a reduced fraction.
            </p>
            <p>
                <m>\frac{8}{9} \div \frac{3}{5} = </m> <var name="$ans" width="10"/>
            </p>
        </statement>
    </webwork>
</exercise>

